    "body": "Long current-location requests offered the correct stored record but entered the inherited dependency path and returned `Unknown.`. This adds a parent-bound signed-H4 selector that accepts that exact current candidate or defers to the unchanged parent. An automatically built lexical-prime dictionary and context bounded by committed source-byte endpoints distinguish current requests from literal words inside facts. Historical selection, stored identities, inner parameters and shared copy/field emission remain intact.\n\nRetain `f0901dad`: 208/208 construction targets with 2,292/2,292 preservation cases; 196/196 independently drawn fresh targets with 568/568 preservation cases. Removing the occurrence scope breaks sixteen factual-word cases; erasing only the new geometric transforms gives 0/196 fresh target answers. Two earlier candidates are preserved as rejected evidence, including one that passed construction but failed fresh transfer. Development was explicitly reopened after that failure; the successor was selected before its separate fresh draw and was not refitted or redrawn.\n\nValidation executed locally:\n- Optimized offline Rust core/API example build; formatting and claim-wording checks.\n- Twelve focused checks, including actual artifact integrity, both rejected-format roundtrips, eight current→historical→arithmetic conversations, 2,064 input/476 output checkpoint positions and 48 malformed-state rejections.\n- 808 actual native API completion/checkpoint-follow-up checks.\n- All 72 query-owner and 216 historical comparisons preserved; fourteen older behavior/control reports have zero checked differences; twelve histories and 24 word/Rust cases preserved.\n- Copy/Add and action each pass 24 ordinary and 24 stress cases. Actual generated Rust compiles and executes.\n\nThe immutable evidence records 2,636.903 model seconds and 805.356 engineering-command seconds, with complete cumulative resource and preservation receipts. Final delivery charges append locally. No unique deletion or paid external compute occurred. Queue CI statuses are compatibility acknowledgements, not tests. Full-suite, HTTP/browser/WASM, allocation instrumentation and complete-path energy checks are NOT_RUN.\n\nThese are bounded authored forms with fresh spellings; general prose, reasoning/program synthesis and alpha/frontier capability remain unfinished. The next observed gap is initial-versus-immediate-previous version selection, requiring temporal intent and bounded ancestor/path validation. The committed source boundary is not general linguistic segmentation.\n\nReferences #973. The writer-context contribution obligation under #1139 remains separate and open.\n",
